58:  About this article (updated October 2026). This article describes the methodology of León, Jemielita, Guo, Marceau West and Anderson (2024), Statistics in Medicine, https://doi.org/10.1002/sim.10163, as the package first implemented it: the split-sample consistency screen evaluated by random half-splits, bootstrap bias correction, and GRF variable-importance screening of the candidate factors. The current package evaluates the consistency screen in closed form (consistency_method = "resample", the default; random half-splitting is only the fallback, so fs.splits has no effect otherwise), reports selection-adjusted estimates and one-sided bounds by multiplier resampling (mr_inference = TRUE; León and Anderson 2026a, arXiv:2609.38361), and calibrates the declaration of a subgroup at a protected level (León and Anderson 2026b, arXiv:2610.28379). The GRF variable-importance screen is removed as of 0.4.1 (vi.grf.min is deprecated and has no effect). The current methodology is documented in vignette("forestsearch") and vignette("survival-post-selection"); the argument listings below are kept for the 2024 workflow and are not the complete current signature of forestsearch() — see ?forestsearch.
914:León, Larry F., and Keaven M. Anderson. 2026a. Inference for Standard Trial Estimands After Data-Driven Subgroup Discovery. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.38361.
916:León, Larry F., and Keaven M. Anderson. 2026b. Interpretable Subgroup Identification Across Survival and Generalized-Linear Outcomes. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2610.28379.
